        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "c22e2203-f085-3afd-bb7a-67e38f7c2d22",
                "word": "vulgarité",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "f74b7f57-0193-4d59-a564-059d848d6c39",
                        "entry_id": "c22e2203-f085-3afd-bb7a-67e38f7c2d22",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "vulgarités"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "281f86d4-e68d-3301-9c8d-21f51eadf4f4",
                        "entry_id": "c22e2203-f085-3afd-bb7a-67e38f7c2d22",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Caractère ou défaut de ce qui est vulgaire ou trivial."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "955f4bc7-aa07-438c-81ce-95d635bc7afb",
                                "sense_id": "281f86d4-e68d-3301-9c8d-21f51eadf4f4",
                                "text": "Ce M. Du Poirier était un être de la dernière vulgarité, et qui semblait fier de ses façons basses et familières ; c’est ainsi que le cochon se vautre dans la fange avec une sorte de volupté insolente pour le spectateur."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "91a50193-c1c9-4636-8ede-191ed990c8f2",
                                "sense_id": "281f86d4-e68d-3301-9c8d-21f51eadf4f4",
                                "text": "De plus en plus ce qui, dans ses rapports avec les hommes, lui répugnait le plus, c'était leur vulgarité, leur souci d'être, de penser et d'agir comme tout le monde, […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "be97dbe1-72a3-45ba-9d40-ba534b232e7f",
                                "sense_id": "281f86d4-e68d-3301-9c8d-21f51eadf4f4",
                                "text": "Une patricienne italienne peut ripoliner la façade de son présidentiel époux, et tenter, en vain, de dissimuler sa confondante vulgarité d’activiste, sa vraie nature pointe toujours."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "84671394-f521-4c4d-98ee-c820bf29e99f",
                                "sense_id": "281f86d4-e68d-3301-9c8d-21f51eadf4f4",
                                "text": "Quand il drague une fille, ce lourdingue qui s'affranchit des codes de la séduction tombe rapidement dans la vulgarité."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f8bdad0a-958d-3a63-a855-f2b21fe0af52",
                        "entry_id": "c22e2203-f085-3afd-bb7a-67e38f7c2d22",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Mot qui est vulgaire, grossier."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "formal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d78574ef-444e-4c8a-9fb8-b90d3c8772b0",
                                "sense_id": "f8bdad0a-958d-3a63-a855-f2b21fe0af52",
                                "text": "Une vulgarité lui a échappé, il le regrette maintenant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4a58cb92-7916-45ed-a8f7-640c653de715",
                                "sense_id": "f8bdad0a-958d-3a63-a855-f2b21fe0af52",
                                "text": "Tu parles ! C’est impossible d’avoir une discussion normale avec lui sans qu’il nous sorte son lot de vulgarités."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "51802a4f-860e-4c65-b242-66cd4fa01e0a",
                        "source_entry_id": "c22e2203-f085-3afd-bb7a-67e38f7c2d22",
                        "source_sense_description": "Caractère de ce qui est vulgaire",
                        "target_lang_word": "vulgarity",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "vulgarity",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9126abd1-8622-3047-8aec-0779a8bd9d0e",
                                        "entry_id": "11e3146d-3b85-33e9-9b08-440d9f07070e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality of being vulgar."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "449f47a7-c7b2-4e7b-9994-ef15f3d24266",
                                                "sense_id": "9126abd1-8622-3047-8aec-0779a8bd9d0e",
                                                "text": "You will observe that I have not yet indulged myself in calling her by that name, even to you. Think, then, what I must have endured in hearing it bandied between the Eltons with all the vulgarity of needless repetition, and all the insolence of imaginary superiority"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2f79a9ed-d960-3bed-9b56-f0725c67b1a2",
                                        "entry_id": "11e3146d-3b85-33e9-9b08-440d9f07070e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An offensive or obscene act or expression."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4c5809a0-1948-4911-8d5b-fd4aa9476271",
                        "source_entry_id": "c22e2203-f085-3afd-bb7a-67e38f7c2d22",
                        "source_sense_description": "Caractère de ce qui est vulgaire",
                        "target_lang_word": "coarseness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "coarseness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0b635064-a2bc-3af3-98b2-a1dd3930dbaa",
                                        "entry_id": "ecbe3876-107f-3c7d-bf5a-8746e5f50786",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The property of being coarse, roughness or primitiveness, unrefined or unpolished."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8cd7a140-ff9b-37e7-ace3-725e2738cabe",
                                        "entry_id": "ecbe3876-107f-3c7d-bf5a-8746e5f50786",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality or state of being coarse"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2683bf7e-5926-4b59-9b76-6886a0916094",
                                                "sense_id": "8cd7a140-ff9b-37e7-ace3-725e2738cabe",
                                                "text": "coarseness of food, texture, manners, or language"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "607560e7-4a2f-4d19-a19f-34a99a5a49a8",
                                                "sense_id": "8cd7a140-ff9b-37e7-ace3-725e2738cabe",
                                                "text": "All this was extraordinarily distasteful to Churchill. It was ugly, gross. […] Never before had he felt such repulsion when the vicar displayed his characteristic bluntness or coarseness of speech. In the present connection—[…]—such talk had been distressingly out of place."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cebaa570-c460-392b-ae1e-af8b655a8e0c",
                                        "entry_id": "ecbe3876-107f-3c7d-bf5a-8746e5f50786",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something that is coarse."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e3dc2a75-9d87-4a48-a0c3-02a3e6c81d62",
                                                "sense_id": "cebaa570-c460-392b-ae1e-af8b655a8e0c",
                                                "text": "This sketch is rather coarse, but probably it is as little exaggerated as could be expected from Walpole. The society which it illustrates abounded with such coarsenesses. Princesses were not expected to exhibit much propriety—nor Duchesses to be overburthened with delicacy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c877d666-0ca6-4749-84cb-b0a6cb5a7699",
                                                "sense_id": "cebaa570-c460-392b-ae1e-af8b655a8e0c",
                                                "text": "Hogarth does not refrain from introducing a sign in his engraving “Noon,” of 1738, showing the Baptist’s head on a charger, with the cynical inscription “Good Eating.” Whether such coarsenesses were actually perpetrated, even under the lax régime of Charles II in England, when frivolity reigned after the fall of Cromwell, it is hard to decide."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a33131a-fcc4-432d-9f6c-cddeb82c5714",
                                                "sense_id": "cebaa570-c460-392b-ae1e-af8b655a8e0c",
                                                "text": "In fact, Angela Lansbury’s bawdy, chattering, equivocal Granny—a super opportunity glintily grasped—is as likely to entertain young Rosaleen with such coarsenesses as ‘. . . and she found another husband not too shy to piss into a pot’ as to scare her with warnings about men whose eyebrows meet: […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4fe76c7e-2070-4f28-8c20-f4cd026333a3",
                        "source_entry_id": "c22e2203-f085-3afd-bb7a-67e38f7c2d22",
